    <statement><p>Give conditions on the constants <m>a</m>, <m>b</m> and <m>c</m> that
ensure that the flux integral <m>\int_S \vec F\cdot d\vec S</m>, where
<m>\vec F=a\vec i +b\vec j+c\vec k</m> and <m>S</m> is the lower half of
the unit sphere centered at the origin and oriented upward, is
negative.</p>
<p><em>(For each, if there is no restriction on the constant
select <alert>=</alert> and enter <alert>anything</alert> for the
value.)</em></p>
<p><m>a</m> <ul form="popup" name="AnSwEr0001"><li>
<p>?</p>
</li><li>
